          "to": "runnin' [n]",
          "note": "Unstressed morpheme-final -ing /ɪŋ/ is realized as [ɪn] or [ən] (spelled -in'); stereotyped in U-RP 'huntin', shootin' and fishin'' and common in casual registers across North American and British accents. Monosyllables such as sing and king are not affected."
